# PROPOSED nanoclaw.service — NOT INSTALLED.
#
# Phase 6 close-out, Part C. This file is a reference copy for review only.
# Nothing in the repo reads it and `npm run setup` does not install it; the
# generator in setup/service.ts writes the unit, and the live unit is at
# /etc/systemd/system/nanoclaw.service.
#
# Installing it is a deliberate, warned step (it needs a nanoclaw restart):
#   cp deploy/nanoclaw.service.proposed /etc/systemd/system/nanoclaw.service
#   # strip these comment lines first if you want the live file to stay terse
#   systemctl daemon-reload
#   systemctl restart nanoclaw        # WARNING: live WhatsApp. Tell Victor first.
#
# Three changes vs. the live unit (see nanoclaw.service.patch):
#
# 1. After=docker.service — follow-up (d). Today the unit only orders itself
#    After=network.target, so on boot NanoClaw can start before dockerd. That
#    is the ordering nondeterminism behind the credential-proxy incident
#    (docker0 absent at start -> bridge detection failed). The code now fails
#    closed to 127.0.0.1 and CREDENTIAL_PROXY_HOST is pinned by an override, so
#    there is no live exposure — this closes the ordering gap itself.
#
# 2. Wants=docker.service — a weak dependency on purpose, not Requires=. With
#    Requires=, a docker.service failure would stop NanoClaw outright, taking
#    WhatsApp down with it; with Wants=, docker is pulled in and ordered first,
#    but NanoClaw still starts and its own ensureContainerRuntimeRunning() can
#    recover the runtime. Note this does NOT make a docker restart safe: ruling
#    2-1 still excludes docker.service from needrestart's automatic restarts.
#
# 3. TimeoutStopSec=330 — the drain bound (NANOCLAW_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS, default
#    300s) plus 30s of headroom, so systemd never SIGKILLs the process in the
#    middle of its own drain. KEEP THESE TWO IN SYNC: if the drain bound is
#    changed, this value must change with it. Drain itself is Part D and is
#    NOT implemented yet — until it is, this unit only means "wait up to 330s
#    for shutdown", which is harmless because today's shutdown returns in
#    well under a second.
#
# KillMode=process is deliberately unchanged: it keeps systemd from killing the
# `docker run` children out from under the drain.
#
# DRIFT WARNING, left for the reviewer to rule on. The unit generator lives in
# setup/service.ts (an inline template string), and setup/service.test.ts holds
# a SECOND, hand-copied duplicate of that template. `npm run setup` rewrites
# /etc/systemd/system/nanoclaw.service from the generator, so re-running setup
# after installing this would silently drop all three lines below. Making the
# change stick means editing the generator too — deliberately NOT done here,
# because it also affects user-level systemd installs (where `docker.service`
# is not a user unit) and fresh non-Linux installs. Options:
#   (a) leave as is and treat `npm run setup` as a known re-break;
#   (b) add the three lines to the generator behind the existing isSystem flag,
#       and de-duplicate the template the test copies.

[Unit]
Description=NanoClaw Personal Assistant
After=network.target docker.service
Wants=docker.service

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=/usr/bin/node /root/nanoclaw/dist/index.js
WorkingDirectory=/root/nanoclaw
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
KillMode=process
TimeoutStopSec=330
Environment=HOME=/root
Environment=PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/root/.local/bin
StandardOutput=append:/root/nanoclaw/logs/nanoclaw.log
StandardError=append:/root/nanoclaw/logs/nanoclaw.error.log

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
